Falsifies `block_roster_contract::read_is_total_and_every_counted_entry_is_gettable`.

The defect: `Roster::read` keeps one entry past the count, `..=count` instead of
`..count`, the off-by-one a reader writes when it thinks of `count` as a last
index. The roster then claims a device the writer never counted (a slot it never
filled), or, on a page with no spare room, slices past the entries it has.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(roster.len(), count as usize, ...)`, on any page the
header accepts with room past its count, or an out-of-bounds slice inside `read`
when the accepted page has exactly `count` entries of room.


diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@
         }
         let (entries, _) = page[HEADER_BYTES..].as_chunks::<ENTRY_BYTES>();
         Ok(Roster {
-            entries: &entries[..count],
+            entries: &entries[..=count],
         })
     }
 
